# Rust build output.
/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Local editor / OS noise.
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# Local-only artifacts. Generated `.flux` modules and connector manifests are *committed and
# reviewed* (see AGENTS.md) — only scratch output and local overrides are ignored here.
/.env
/scratch/
*.local.toml

# Docs site (web/). The Node toolchain is contained under `web/`; only its dependencies and build
# output are ignored — `web/package-lock.json` is committed so CI installs the same tree.
# No trailing slash, deliberately: a trailing slash ignores a *directory* only, so a `node_modules`
# that is a **symlink** — which is how a second worktree usually gets its dependencies — is not
# ignored and `git add -A web/` stages it as a mode-120000 blob holding a machine-absolute path.
# That happened once (C-100): it dangles on every other machine, and checking it out over a
# populated directory asks git to replace that directory with a link to itself.
/web/node_modules
/web/.vitepress/dist/
/web/.vitepress/cache/

# The host's operator page (C-239). A second, separate Node tree — deliberately not `web/`'s, since
# the public site is forbidden to collect a credential and this page exists to collect one. Same
# rule as above: the lockfile is committed so CI installs the same tree, `node_modules` is not, and
# no trailing slash so a symlinked one is still ignored.
/crates/connectors-api/ui/node_modules

# Agent worktrees (harness-owned, never tracked)
.claude/
